#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# not

#% text
# `not(a)`, written `not a`, is the logical negation of a truth value.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The negation of a comparison is the opposite comparison: `not x > y` is `x <= y`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
not true
#% output
#= false

#% cell
not (1 > 2)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
not x > y
#% output
#= x <= y

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Double negation cancels:

#% cell
not not a
#% output
#= a

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `and`, `or`, `unequal`
